# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-16, 2.1-F6). L §5.19 Stated parts: "no two of them overlap (a party and a batch at a place
# that keeps pairs, or a party or a batch and a pair that holds it), ... LOAD-PARTS otherwise"; L §8.3 LOAD-PARTS
# `the stated parts <q> and <q'> of <x> overlap`. ania and a1 at a place both owned and batched.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  batched
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order k.batch.day
kind tomeks: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of a1, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of (tomek, a1)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-01
  anchor konto
  stated[konto] = 150.00 PLN at 2026-03-31 end
  stated[konto] of ania = 50.00 PLN at 2026-03-31 end
  stated[konto] of a1 = 50.00 PLN at 2026-03-31 end
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARTS the stated parts ania and a1 of konto overlap (m.tally:48)
